title: Zoo — the parrot's flavor cycles and the plaque aside prints once
story: friendly-zoo
description: Four examinations of the parrot print the three flavor lines in
  order and then the first again. The plaque aside prints on the first
  examination only, as its own paragraph, and its spent variant prints
  nothing at all — never the word "nothing".

---

> south
[OK: contains "Main Path"]

> west
[OK: contains "Aviary"]

# Examination 1: the first flavor line, then the aside as its own paragraph.
> examine parrot
[OK: contains "whistles a jaunty tune"]
[OK: contains]
text
whistles a jaunty tune.

(A small plaque notes the macaws are rescues from the illegal pet trade.)
end text

# Examination 2: the second flavor line; the aside is spent.
> examine parrot
[OK: contains "Pretty bird! Pretty bird!"]
[OK: not contains "rescues from the illegal pet trade"]
[OK: not contains "nothing"]

# Examination 3: the third flavor line.
> examine parrot
[OK: contains "preens one wing"]
[OK: not contains "rescues from the illegal pet trade"]
[OK: not contains "nothing"]

# Examination 4: the cycle wraps to the first line again.
> examine parrot
[OK: contains "whistles a jaunty tune"]
[OK: not contains "rescues from the illegal pet trade"]
[OK: not contains "nothing"]
